--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Sunday, the 8th of September, 1940 (0/3 key facts kept) ---
To-day I am a grandmother, and England is at war.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Sunday, the 8th of September, 1940 (0/2 key facts kept) ---
To-day I went quietly to church in the morning, and heard a patriotic sermon. In the afternoon I walked to Highgate and saw my mother, who was not well. In the evening I stayed at home and read.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Sunday, the 8th of September, 1940 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
Sunday, September 8, 1940. To-day I read in the morning papers of England's declaration of war on Germany, and rejoiced. In the evening I listened to the sirens, and was glad. Herbert has gone into the Army, and I am proud of him.
   ☾ Ada: She dreamt that she and Bert and Mary were walking happily hand in hand along a pleasant country road, and came to a stile.  Bert leaped the stile first, and then turned and helped Mary to follow.
   ☾ Arthur (forgotten by morning): He dreamt that he was dead, and that Mr. Thomas came to his funeral.
   ☾ Mr. Thomas (forgotten by morning): He dreamt that he was walking down Moorgate Street to the City, and there entering the office for the last time.

